{"availability":"available","full":"frankmcsherry/datatoad","name":"datatoad","description":"An interactive Datalog","category":"Other","language":"Rust","stars":79,"forks":7,"created":"2025-06-13T21:57:13Z","updated":"2026-09-20T21:00:54Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"http://www.frankmcsherry.org/datatoad/","topics":[],"demo":"http://www.frankmcsherry.org/datatoad/demo/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T16:06:28.803Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T16:06:28.803Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T16:06:28.803Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T16:06:28.803Z","stars":79,"forks":7}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["An interactive, columnar, worst-case optimal Datalog","📖 Read the book · 🐸 Try it in your browser (datatoad compiled to WebAssembly, running client-side)","Datalog is a logic programming language whose evaluation is most commonly based on repeated application of relational equijoins. A Datalog program is a collection of rules, each of which describes conditions under which some facts being true leads to other facts being true. When combined with a starting set of facts, rules lead to an iterative process in which more facts can be inferred, iteratively, until eventually no additional facts can be learned."],"features":["It is interactive in that the user supplies their logic program to our interpreter program, which evaluates it without additional compilation.","It is columnar in that the evaluator is column-oriented and avoids any row-at-a-time operation.","It is worst-case optimal in the sense that its multi-way join implementations parallel an instance of the Generic Join framework."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/frankmcsherry/datatoad/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"5f2590982d0908c2a492c5a619feb09bf0dd7364cb0532fecd1f416556a7dd31","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T16:06:28.893Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T16:06:28.893Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text